00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:27.400
shortlist, resumes based on the JD, this is your task

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:31.400
first of all this task will go to the planner mode

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:35.400
now in planner mode there is a LLM

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:39.400
this LLM will take the task

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:43.400
and make a detailed plan

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:47.400
what does it mean?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:51.400
LLM will understand the task and its intent

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:55.400
and LLM also has an idea of the tools

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:59.400
that is, what resources are available

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:03.400
to do this task, this is also the knowledge of LLM

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:07.400
so take the task from one side and the tools from the other side

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:11.400
and understand which tools can you use to execute this task

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.400
and which tools can you use to reach the final output

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.400
and around that this LLM, this planner node LLM

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:23.400
will make a detailed plan

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.400
and this plan will also be made according to my steps

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.400
means in this plan we will have a list of steps

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:35.400
like you will have bulleted steps

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.400
like step 1, step 2, step 3, according to the bullet points

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:43.400
and for this planning node I am using

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:47.400
a structured output LLM

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.400
which basically will take my task

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:55.400
and the tools and the plan that it will generate

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:59.400
it will be a series or a list of steps

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:03.400
